# Keep the Vercel deploy a pure STATIC build.
#
# The key line is `app.py`: it is the Streamlit entrypoint, not a serverless
# function. If uploaded, Vercel's zero-config Python runtime tries to build it
# as a WSGI/ASGI function and fails with:
#   "Found app.py but it does not export a top-level app/application/handler".
# Excluding it (and requirements.txt) stops that auto-detection.
#
# NOTE: files the build step needs must NOT be listed here —
#   build_web.py, stockdash/, sample_data/, requirements-build.txt, web/

app.py
requirements.txt
generate_sample_data.py
tests/
.github/
README.md
*.png
*.log
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
